Q: Get the value from the mat-input in angular material A: <p>Use the name also Something like</p>
<pre><code>&lt;mat-form-field appearance=&quot;fill&quot;&gt;
    &lt;form&gt;
       &lt;mat-label&gt;Insert Anything&lt;/mat-label&gt;
       &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot;  matInput [(ngModel)] =&quot;oName&quot; name=&quot;oName&quot; &gt;
       &lt;mat-hint&gt;Serie&lt;/mat-hint&gt;
    &lt;/form&gt;
&lt;/mat-form-field&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: How to add more data an array of objects in a lightning component A: <p>Use this code snippet when getting values from the server</p>
<pre><code>var state = response.getState();
if (state === 'SUCCESS'){

  var result = response.getReturnValue()
  var objs = [];
  var i;
  for (i = 0; i &lt; result.length; i++) {
      objs.push(this.createObj(result[i][0], result[i][1]));
  }//next
  cmp.set(&quot;v.objs&quot;, objs);

}//endif state


createObj: function(theId, theName) {
    var obj = new Object();
    obj.Id = theId;
    obj.Name = theName;
    return obj;
},
</code></pre>

Q: How can I use Microsoft Entra on a GitHub Page for an Azure Function? A: <p>Your Issuer URL is pinned to <code>9188040d-6c67-4c5b-b112-36a304b66dad</code>, which is the personal Microsoft account tenant, while the app registration is set to &quot;Any Microsoft Entra directory &amp; personal Microsoft accounts&quot;.</p>
<p>Either change the issuer to <code>https://login.microsoftonline.com/common/v2.0</code> and set <code>requestedAccessTokenVersion</code> to 2 in the app manifest, or lock the registration down to a single tenant</p>
<p>also, delete <code>useFunctionToken()</code>. The <code>/.auth/login/aad</code> endpoint exists to hand you a cookie based browser session and you do not need it when you are sending bearer tokens. Replace <code>skipFunctionToken()</code> with below <code>callFunction()</code></p>
<pre><code>async function callFunction() {
  const request = {
    scopes: [&quot;api://74bcc144-d7ca-4448-b88c-ed901f14012d/RunFunction&quot;],
    account: msalAccount
  };
  let response;
  try {
    response = await ms.auth.acquireTokenSilent(request);
  } catch (e) {
    response = await ms.auth.acquireTokenPopup(request);
  }
  const result = await fetch(
    &quot;https://vm-member-site-auth-bze3bqebc2b7btca.eastus2-01.azurewebsites.net/api/VMMembersAuth&quot;,
    { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${response.accessToken}` } }
  );
  console.log(result.status, await result.text());
}
</code></pre>
